{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789498650,"nonce":"C2fhfg9pDKtEikUQXFIz++v6MBE=","title":"while/else in fannkuch","message":"The unedited PyPy fannkuch kernel advances past bound method values and list slice assignment, then zypy reports `while/else is not supported yet` on its `while r != n: ... else: return max_flips`. Python runs the else suite only when the loop condition ends it, not on `break`; zero iterations also run else. A minimal reproducer:\n\n    x = 0\n    while x \u003c 1:\n        x += 1\n    else:\n        print(\"done\")\n\n    while True:\n        break\n    else:\n        print(\"wrong\")\n\nNested loop breaks must affect only their own loop. Continue must not suppress else. A break redirected through try/finally needs its final control action reflected. Related: statement forms 2bdf9f4 and speed-center index 89aaf85.","files":null}]}